body:
As mentioned in RC, I would rather modify `BIND_ENUM_CONSTANT` to re-use the class registered there.

The reason is that it's supposed to match anyway, so by not matching automatically we're creating a new footgun.

The following (or something similar) should work:

```c++
template <typename T>
inline StringName __constant_get_enum_value_name(const char *p_name) {
    // May need to prefix the enum name with "::" here, not sure how else the identifier is used.
	return String(p_name).get_slice("::", 1);
}
```

```c++
#define BIND_ENUM_CONSTANT(m_constant) \
	::ClassDB::bind_integer_constant(get_class_static(), __constant_get_enum_name(m_constant), __constant_get_enum_value_name(m_constant), m_constant);
```

