This feels a bit wrong to me. Could we make a BIND_ENUM_CONSTANT_EXT instead like we did for variant enum cast? Which would look like this:

```cpp
#define BIND_ENUM_CONSTANT_EXT(m_constant, m_bound_name) \
	::ClassDB::bind_integer_constant(get_class_static(), __constant_get_enum_name(m_constant), #m_bound_name, m_constant);


BIND_ENUM_CONSTANT_EXT(RenderingDeviceEnums::DEVICE_TYPE_OTHER, DEVICE_TYPE_OTHER);
```

